  "system": {
    "description": {
      "type": "String",
      "label": "Description",
      "value": "<p> A piece of shrapnel takes a large fragment off your tibia, the long weight-bearing bone of your lower leg. The new structural weakness quickly makes itself felt as your weight causes the tibia to snap, a broken-off jagged end tearing out through the skin, sending you crashing to the ground howling with pain.</p> <p><strong>Effects:</strong> Gain @Condition[Stunned] (3) and @Condition[Prone]. The leg is useless (see under Amputated Parts), and will remain so unless your receive Surgery within a week. If you do it’ll count as a Broken Bone (Major), except any Test for long-term penalties automatically fail. Regardless, you also contract a Festering Wound due to the open fracture.</p>"
    },
